\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Payload audit of real serialized update sizes. Frozen-$A$ clients upload only the trainable $B$ factor (1{,}408 parameters per rank column); the $A{+}B$ column is the joint-training equivalent. The stylized $s(r)$ column lists the protocol reused as a normalized-cost cell in the simulation study. The ceiling grid bills a rank-2 update at 0.02\,MB against a true 0.011\,MB (a 77\% inflation, versus 11\% at rank 16), a conservative bias shared by every scheduled method; the grid sweep bounds the induced error.}}{10}{table.70}\protected@file@percent }
