\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The strong-backbone stress regime in the single currency. (a)~Accuracy trajectories and (b)~accuracy against cumulative delivered update mass (\cref  {sec:main}, terminal protocol as everywhere): every LoRA policy sits at backbone parity, FedRAS reaches it along the steepest capacity path, and the flat full-model curve is the zero-communication control realized---nothing delivered, no learning.}}{12}{figure.87}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:capview}{{4}{12}{The strong-backbone stress regime in the single currency. (a)~Accuracy trajectories and (b)~accuracy against cumulative delivered update mass (\cref {sec:main}, terminal protocol as everywhere): every LoRA policy sits at backbone parity, FedRAS reaches it along the steepest capacity path, and the flat full-model curve is the zero-communication control realized---nothing delivered, no learning}{figure.87}{}}
\newlabel{fig:capview@cref}{{[figure][4][]4}{[1][12][]12}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The capacity--delivery exchange in one picture. (a)~Supply: the measured delivered-update norm grows with the square root of the rank (the anchor of \cref  {eq:cap}). (b)~Price: the payload-conditioned delivery probability of \cref  {eq:hazard} per SAGIN link class at the 0.1\,s deadline, at each class's median rate and mean mobility. (c)~Law: the product $\sqrt  {r/r_{\max }}\,\hat  P_{\rm  on}(r)$ peaks at the closed form $r^\star $ of \cref  {eq:rstar} (triangles; ground peaks at the provisioned width), and the diamonds are the trainer's measured per-class delivered ranks in the grouped-profile stress runs, tracking the peaks. (d)~Conversion: the accuracy value of preserved capacity as the backbone weakens (\cref  {sec:weakbb}); the gain vanishes on the strong backbone and grows as adaptation becomes scarce.}}{13}{figure.89}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:exchange}{{5}{13}{The capacity--delivery exchange in one picture. (a)~Supply: the measured delivered-update norm grows with the square root of the rank (the anchor of \cref {eq:cap}). (b)~Price: the payload-conditioned delivery probability of \cref {eq:hazard} per SAGIN link class at the 0.1\,s deadline, at each class's median rate and mean mobility. (c)~Law: the product $\sqrt {r/r_{\max }}\,\hat P_{\rm on}(r)$ peaks at the closed form $r^\star $ of \cref {eq:rstar} (triangles; ground peaks at the provisioned width), and the diamonds are the trainer's measured per-class delivered ranks in the grouped-profile stress runs, tracking the peaks. (d)~Conversion: the accuracy value of preserved capacity as the backbone weakens (\cref {sec:weakbb}); the gain vanishes on the strong backbone and grows as adaptation becomes scarce}{figure.89}{}}
\newlabel{fig:exchange@cref}{{[figure][5][]5}{[1][12][]13}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces The closed form \cref  {eq:rstar} against the trainer's actual assignments in the grouped-profile stress runs (0.1\,s, five seeds, 2000 client--round points, one dot per assignment with vertical jitter). Assignments track $r_i^\star $ across all three link classes; the nearest-candidate reading of the closed form reproduces the assigned rank on about three quarters of the points, and the remainder sits one step below at candidate boundaries, where the discrete argmax is slightly conservative.}}{13}{figure.91}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rstar}{{6}{13}{The closed form \cref {eq:rstar} against the trainer's actual assignments in the grouped-profile stress runs (0.1\,s, five seeds, 2000 client--round points, one dot per assignment with vertical jitter). Assignments track $r_i^\star $ across all three link classes; the nearest-candidate reading of the closed form reproduces the assigned rank on about three quarters of the points, and the remainder sits one step below at candidate boundaries, where the discrete argmax is slightly conservative}{figure.91}{}}
\newlabel{fig:rstar@cref}{{[figure][6][]6}{[1][12][]13}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Delivered-update norm vs.\ rank on CIFAR-10 (mean over delivered rounds; five seeds per point, error bars are one standard deviation). The measured growth ($2.5\times $ from rank 2 to 16, $1.9\times $ from rank 4 to 16) tracks the square-root capacity law of \cref  {eq:cap} ($2.8\times $ and $2.0\times $) rather than linear payload growth ($8\times $ and $4\times $); the nominal and stress series coincide.}}{13}{figure.93}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:normlaw}{{7}{13}{Delivered-update norm vs.\ rank on CIFAR-10 (mean over delivered rounds; five seeds per point, error bars are one standard deviation). The measured growth ($2.5\times $ from rank 2 to 16, $1.9\times $ from rank 4 to 16) tracks the square-root capacity law of \cref {eq:cap} ($2.8\times $ and $2.0\times $) rather than linear payload growth ($8\times $ and $4\times $); the nominal and stress series coincide}{figure.93}{}}
\newlabel{fig:normlaw@cref}{{[figure][7][]7}{[1][12][]13}}
